course: dictionary
lesson: 3940
title: The ending -ful
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Ful» on its own is not an English word. It is a fragment: a piece that only works when it is joined to the end of another word. The ending is spelled -ful, with one l, and it means «full of» or «having».
explain: Add -ful to a word and you get a describing word: hope becomes hopeful, which means full of hope, and care becomes careful, which means full of care. Add it to a container word like spoon or cup and you get an amount: a spoonful, a cupful.
explain: Watch your spelling. It is «beautiful», not «beautifull», even though full has two l's. When a word ends in y, change the y to i first: beauty becomes beautiful, pity becomes pitiful. If you see «ful» on its own in a text, it is probably a typing mistake for «full».
fact: The suffix -ful means full of or having: hopeful, colourful, helpful.
fact: Added to a container word, -ful makes an amount: a spoonful, a handful, a cupful, a mouthful.
fact: The suffix -ful has only one l, even though the word full has two.
fact: When a word ends in y, change the y to i before adding -ful: beauty becomes beautiful.
fact: On its own, «ful» is not a word in English. It is a fragment, or a spelling mistake for «full».
exercise: «The helpful dog fetched the ball.» What does -ful add to help? | Under the ball | *Full of help, so giving help | Not helping at all | Very quickly
exercise: Which word is spelled correctly? | *beautiful | beautifuly | beautifull | beutiful
exercise: «She asked for a spoonful of sugar.» What does spoonful mean? | A spoon with a handle | A kind of spoon for soup | A spoon that is full of holes | *As much as a spoon can hold
test: Add -ful to hope. What word do you make? | hopfull | *hopeful | hopefull | hopeing
test: Add -ful to pity, changing the y first. What word do you make? | pityful | pitty-full | pitifull | *pitiful
exam: Which meaning fits the ending -ful in «careful»? | Like a careless child | Without care | Done by a cat | *Full of care
